.TH SDL_SetWindowOpacity 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_SetWindowOpacity \- Set the opacity for a window.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_video.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_SetWindowOpacity(SDL_Window *window, float opacity);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The parameter
.BR opacity
will be clamped internally between 0\[char46]0f (transparent) and 1\[char46]0f (opaque)\[char46]
.PP
This function also returns false if setting the opacity isn\(aqt supported\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I window
the window which will be made transparent or opaque\[char46]
.TP
.I opacity
the opacity value (0\[char46]0f - transparent, 1\[char46]0f - opaque)\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should only be called on the main thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_GetWindowOpacity (3)
